  "modelingNotes": [
    "Charlotte Douglas International Airport (CLT): Concourses B and C — procedural, CC0-1.0.",
    "The two piers running south-west and south-east from the Atrium: long two-level gate concourses whose walls jog out at each gate. The OSM outlines (way/1347416913, way/1347416955) are extruded to the 8 m their building:parts record, with the gate-level windows as a band of slate panels, a pale roof, and a low glazed vault down the middle of each over the central walkway.",
    "Mapbox's 3D buildings (tileset mapbox.mapbox-3dbuildings-v1), used only as a visual reference, put both roofs at 7.5-9.5 m and show nothing standing much above them, so the vault is kept low: a 0.6 m curb and a 1.4 m rise, rather than the 2 m clerestory and 2.6 m vault of the first version.",
    "Site frame and helpers: see clt-terminal.ts.",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"clt-concourses-b-c\", model \"clt-concourses-b-c\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/c3921f733df14b41e1f6d15853cce7b343886f17/generators/clt-concourses-b-c.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches."
  ],
